    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nI took a default and made it configurable.\r\n\r\nI utilize this in my own config of mini.bufremove:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n{\r\n  \"echasnovski/mini.bufremove\",\r\n  dev = true, -- Remove once PR is accepted\r\n  opts = {\r\n    on_delete_last_fallback = function(_)\r\n      local orig_cwd = os.getenv(\"PWD\")\r\n      vim.fn.chdir(orig_cwd)\r\n      vim.cmd(\"SessionDelete\")\r\n      vim.cmd(\"Alpha\")\r\n    end,\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```",
    "closed_at": "2023-09-05T18:05:14Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nI'd rather not introduce this functionality instead suggesting to write own wrappers using exported functions. Something [like this](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/249#issuecomment-1452431730).\r\n\r\nIn your case it can be something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal open_starter_if_empty_buffer = function()\r\n  local is_empty = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0) == \"\" and vim.bo.filetype == ''\r\n  if not is_empty then return end\r\n\r\n  local orig_cwd = os.getenv(\"PWD\")\r\n  vim.fn.chdir(orig_cwd)\r\n  vim.cmd(\"SessionDelete\")\r\n  require('mini.starter').open()\r\nend\r\n\r\n_G.my_bufdelete = function(...)\r\n  require('mini.bufremove').delete(...)\r\n  open_starter_if_empty_buffer()\r\nend\r\n\r\n_G.my_bufwipeout = function(...)\r\n  require('mini.bufremove').wipeout(...)\r\n  open_starter_if_empty_buffer()\r\nend\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2023-09-05T18:05:14Z",
