        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I still have a problem with a dangling '[No Name]' buffer, created by `require(\"mini.bufremove\").delete(...)`.\r\n\r\nI tried out the following:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n{\r\n  \"echasnovski/mini.bufremove\",\r\n  keys = {\r\n    {\r\n      \"<leader>bd\",\r\n      function(...)\r\n        require(\"mini.bufremove\").delete(...)\r\n        local is_empty = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0) == \"\" and vim.bo.filetype == \"\"\r\n        if not is_empty then\r\n          return\r\n        end\r\n\r\n        -- vim.api.nvim_buf_delete(0, {}) -- desperate times...\r\n        local orig_cwd = os.getenv(\"PWD\")\r\n        vim.fn.chdir(orig_cwd)\r\n        vim.cmd(\"SessionDelete\")\r\n        vim.cmd(\"Alpha\")\r\n      end,\r\n      desc = \"Delete Buffer\",\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```",
